msgid "**Executor:**\n"
msgstr "**Executor:**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"circuit-samplex\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Replace PUB tuples with a `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Langkah 3. Ganti tuple PUB dengan `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of passing a list of tuples (PUBs), when using Executor, you build a `QuantumProgram` and append _items_ to it.\n"
msgstr "Alih-alih meneruskan daftar tuple (PUB), saat menggunakan Executor, kamu membangun `QuantumProgram` dan menambahkan _item_ ke dalamnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `QuantumProgram` accepts _circuit_ items and _samplex_ items:\n"
msgstr "`QuantumProgram` menerima item _circuit_ dan item _samplex_:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Appends a `CircuitItem`, which is a circuit and (optionally) its\n"
"parameter values. It is executed as-is, without any randomization. \n"
msgstr ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Menambahkan `CircuitItem`, yaitu sebuah circuit dan (secara opsional) nilai\n"
"parameternya. Item ini dieksekusi apa adanya, tanpa randomisasi apa pun. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this when you just want to sample a circuit, exactly as Sampler would with a PUB that has no\n"
"  twirling; for example, when submitting a plain sampling job, or when you already manually included any\n"
"  variants you want.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Appends a `samplexItem`, which is a *template circuit* plus a\n"
"  *samplex* that generates randomized parameter sets on the server side. \n"
msgstr ""
"  Gunakan ini ketika kamu hanya ingin mengambil sampel circuit, persis seperti yang dilakukan Sampler dengan PUB yang tidak memiliki\n"
"  twirling; misalnya, saat mengirimkan job sampling biasa, atau saat kamu sudah menyertakan secara manual\n"
"  varian yang kamu inginkan.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Menambahkan `samplexItem`, yaitu sebuah *template circuit* ditambah\n"
"  *samplex* yang menghasilkan set parameter acak di sisi server. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this\n"
"  when you want the circuit's content randomized. The primary case is with \n"
"  twirling (gate or measurement) or noise injection. This capability replaces\n"
"  Sampler's built-in twirling.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Gunakan ini\n"
"  ketika kamu ingin konten circuit diacak. Kasus utamanya adalah dengan \n"
"  twirling (gate atau measurement) atau noise injection. Kemampuan ini menggantikan\n"
"  twirling bawaan Sampler.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single `QuantumProgram` can accept both item types; each appended item is executed as an\n"
"independent task and produces its own entry in the results. In general, use `append_circuit_item` when your circuit does not need to be randomized. Otherwise, use `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah `QuantumProgram` bisa menerima kedua jenis item; setiap item yang ditambahkan dieksekusi sebagai\n"
"tugas independen dan menghasilkan entri sendiri di hasil. Secara umum, gunakan `append_circuit_item` ketika circuitmu tidak perlu diacak. Jika tidak, gunakan `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next sections show each in turn: parameterized circuits that use \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, and migrating twirling by using `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian selanjutnya menunjukkan masing-masing secara berurutan: circuit berparameter yang menggunakan \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, dan migrasi twirling dengan menggunakan `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following code examples, `isa_circuit` refers to the circuit that has been transpiled to conform to the target backend's [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA). This `isa_circuit` contains two parameters.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh kode berikut, `isa_circuit` mengacu pada circuit yang telah ditranspilasi agar sesuai dengan [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA) backend target. `isa_circuit` ini berisi dua parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"param-circuits\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3a. Migrate parameterized circuits {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"
msgstr "Langkah 3a. Migrasi circuit berparameter {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Sampler, parameter values are the second element of the PUB tuple. With Executor,\n"
"pass them as `circuit_arguments` to `append_circuit_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan Sampler, nilai parameter merupakan elemen kedua dari tuple PUB. Dengan Executor,\n"
"teruskan nilai tersebut sebagai `circuit_arguments` ke `append_circuit_item`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor**\n"
msgstr "**Executor**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3b. Migrate built-in twirling to explicit annotations {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"
msgstr "Langkah 3b. Migrasi twirling bawaan ke anotasi eksplisit {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the most significant change. Sampler applies twirling for you by using options. With \n"
"Executor, you declare that intent explicitly by using annotated boxes and\n"
"a samplex (from [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah perubahan paling signifikan. Sampler menerapkan twirling untukmu dengan menggunakan opsi. Dengan \n"
"Executor, kamu mendeklarasikan maksud tersebut secara eksplisit dengan menggunakan box beranotasi dan\n"
"samplex (dari [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler (twirling by using options):**\n"
msgstr "**Sampler (twirling dengan menggunakan opsi):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor (twirling by using boxes and a samplex):**\n"
msgstr "**Executor (twirling dengan menggunakan box dan samplex):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the template circuit and samplex are built on the client side, you can\n"
"inspect and sample them locally to verify the output before sending anything to\n"
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena template circuit dan samplex dibangun di sisi client, kamu bisa\n"
"memeriksa dan mengambil sampelnya secara lokal untuk memverifikasi output sebelum mengirim apa pun ke\n"
"hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-local\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification: Sample the template circuit locally {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"
msgstr "Verifikasi: Ambil sampel template circuit secara lokal {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can draw randomizations from the samplex and bind them to the template\n"
"circuit to confirm that the samplex is producing the parameter values you expect.\n"
"The parameter values returned by `samplex.sample` are directly compatible with the\n"
"template circuit's parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu bisa menarik randomisasi dari samplex dan mengikatnya ke template\n"
"circuit untuk memastikan bahwa samplex menghasilkan nilai parameter yang kamu harapkan.\n"
"Nilai parameter yang dikembalikan oleh `samplex.sample` secara langsung kompatibel dengan\n"
"parameter template circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To go further, you can verify that each randomization is logically equivalent to the\n"
"original circuit by, for example, converting both to `Operator` objects and comparing their unitary implementations (after\n"
"accounting for the `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` corrections that undo\n"
"measurement twirling), or by comparing expectation values from a local\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` or `StatevectorEstimator` run. See the Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"guide for a complete walkthrough.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk lebih lanjut, kamu bisa memverifikasi bahwa setiap randomisasi secara logis setara dengan\n"
"circuit asli, misalnya, dengan mengonversi keduanya menjadi objek `Operator` dan membandingkan implementasi unitary-nya (setelah\n"
"memperhitungkan koreksi `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` yang membatalkan\n"
"twirling measurement), atau dengan membandingkan expectation value dari `StatevectorSampler`\n"
"atau `StatevectorEstimator` lokal yang dijalankan. Lihat panduan Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"untuk penjelasan lengkap.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shots\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Change how shots are requested {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"
msgstr "Langkah 4. Ubah cara shot diminta {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move shots from the PUB to `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  In Executor, `shots` applies to the whole job. Submit multiple jobs if you need different shot counts.\n"
msgstr "Pindahkan shot dari PUB ke `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  Di Executor, `shots` berlaku untuk seluruh job. Kirimkan beberapa job jika kamu membutuhkan jumlah shot yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"options\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5. Update options as necessary {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"
msgstr "Langkah 5. Perbarui opsi sesuai kebutuhan {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are fewer options available to Executor than Sampler, because\n"
"error-mitigation choices now live in your annotations and samplex instead of options.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada lebih sedikit opsi yang tersedia untuk Executor dibandingkan Sampler, karena\n"
"pilihan mitigasi error kini berada di anotasi dan samplex-mu, bukan di opsi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also a structural difference in where settings live. \n"
msgstr "Ada juga perbedaan struktural dalam di mana pengaturan berada. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Sampler,\n"
"everything, including choices that affect result post-processing, is configured on\n"
"the primitive's options or in the PUB. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Dengan Sampler,\n"
"semuanya, termasuk pilihan yang memengaruhi post-processing hasil, dikonfigurasi di\n"
"opsi primitive atau di PUB. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Executor, choices that affect how the job\n"
"results are shaped and post-processed are set on the [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), not on\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Dengan Executor, pilihan yang memengaruhi bagaimana hasil\n"
"job dibentuk dan diproses ditetapkan di [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), bukan di\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples:\n"
msgstr "Examples:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) holds only lower-level execution and environment\n"
"settings that don't change the structure of the returned data. It has three top-level groups:\n"
msgstr ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) hanya menyimpan pengaturan eksekusi dan environment tingkat rendah\n"
"yang tidak mengubah struktur data yang dikembalikan. Ada tiga grup tingkat atas:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"
msgstr "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Contains fewer options than with Sampler.  For example, there  is no `meas_type` Executor option. \n"
msgstr "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Berisi lebih sedikit opsi dibandingkan Sampler.  Misalnya, tidak ada opsi `meas_type` Executor. \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"
msgstr "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notably, the `twirling` and `dynamical_decoupling` options exist in Sampler but not Executor. Instead, those option values are expressed through the directed execution model.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diketahui bahwa opsi `twirling` dan `dynamical_decoupling` ada di Sampler tetapi tidak di Executor. Sebagai gantinya, nilai opsi tersebut diekspresikan melalui directed execution model.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example:**\n"
msgstr "**Example:**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-job\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 6. Update the `run` command {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"
msgstr "Langkah 6. Perbarui perintah `run` {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The input to an Executor job is the program, instead of PUBs.\n"
msgstr "Input untuk job Executor adalah program, bukan PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 7. Change how you access results {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"
msgstr "Langkah 7. Ubah cara kamu mengakses hasil {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Executor, results are NumPy arrays, not `BitArray` objects.  Use the name string as the index (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) and get an `np.ndarray` back. There is no need to remember the `.data.<register>` attribute path.\n"
msgstr "Di Executor, hasil berupa array NumPy, bukan objek `BitArray`.  Gunakan string nama sebagai indeks (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) dan dapatkan `np.ndarray` sebagai hasilnya. Kamu tidak perlu mengingat path atribut `.data.<register>`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To update from Sampler to Executor, change `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` to `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, then rewrite `get_counts`-based post-processing as NumPy operations.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memperbarui dari Sampler ke Executor, ubah `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` menjadi `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, lalu tulis ulang post-processing berbasis `get_counts` sebagai operasi NumPy.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sampler's `BitArray` offers helpers (`get_counts`, `slice_bits`, `slice_shots`, `expectation_values`, and post-selection masks). Executor returns raw NumPy arrays so you can perform this post-processing with standard NumPy operations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirled-results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 8. Handle twirled results (bit-flip corrections) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"
msgstr "Langkah 8. Menangani hasil twirled (koreksi bit-flip) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you apply measurement twirling through a `SamplexItem`, Executor returns the raw\n"
"(twirled) measurements plus the bit-flip corrections needed to undo the twirling.\n"
"You need to apply them manually; nothing is corrected implicitly. \n"
msgstr ""
"Saat kamu menerapkan measurement twirling melalui `SamplexItem`, Executor mengembalikan pengukuran mentah\n"
"(twirled) beserta koreksi bit-flip yang diperlukan untuk membatalkan twirling.\n"
"Kamu perlu menerapkannya secara manual; tidak ada yang dikoreksi secara implisit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using Executor, undo twirling explicitly by using the `measurement_flips.<reg>` corrections and an XOR, as shown in the following example:\n"
msgstr "Saat menggunakan Executor, batalkan twirling secara eksplisit dengan menggunakan koreksi `measurement_flips.<reg>` dan XOR, seperti yang ditunjukkan pada contoh berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no equivalent step in Sampler because it undoes twirling for you.\n"
msgstr "Tidak ada langkah setara di Sampler karena ia membatalkan twirling untukmu secara otomatis.\n"

